<article class="env-exercise" id="02A5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02A5">Exercise <span data-tag="02A5">111.37.9</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a graded ring. Let $X = \text{Proj}(S)$. Let $Z, Z' \subset X$ be two closed subschemes. Let $\varphi : Z \to Z'$ be an isomorphism. Assume $Z \cap Z' = \emptyset $. Show that for any $z \in Z$ there exists an affine open $U \subset X$ such that $z \in U$, $\varphi (z) \in U$ and $\varphi (Z \cap U) = Z' \cap U$. (Hint: Use Exercise <a href="/tag/02A4" data-tag="02A4">111.37.8</a> and something akin to Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01IW" data-tag="01IW">26.11.5</a>.) </p>
</article>